{"title":"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Video_solution_by_grogg007\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video solution by grogg007</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Substitution)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Substitution)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Cancellation)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Cancellation)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Freddy the frog is jumping around the coordinate plane searching for a river, which lies on the horizontal line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/d/a4d8df057b84acc451382bbaad898c70b21eae1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" />. A fence is located at the horizontal line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/0/7a06334068417b1781d14e8b28af827907961eb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" />. On each jump Freddy randomly chooses a direction parallel to one of the coordinate axes and moves one unit in that direction. When he is at a point where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec89f09c84538ec43930ca5d8e5e0957e2000822.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />, with equal likelihoods he chooses one of three directions where he either jumps parallel to the fence or jumps away from the fence, but he never chooses the direction that would have him cross over the fence to where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/8/d98424e07dba484162112ed0575862bd8fcf880b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" />. Freddy starts his search at the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/a/c2a4a6c609d068c8d81c8ddb4ecf8a8d70d1ab68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, 21)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"18\" /> and will stop once he reaches a point on the river. Find the expected number of jumps it will take Freddy to reach the river.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_solution_by_grogg007\">Video solution by <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:grogg007\">grogg007</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Video solution by grogg007\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lDqHL-onoiw\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lDqHL-onoiw</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Substitution.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Substitution)\">Solution 1 (Substitution)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Substitution)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Clearly Freddy's <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-coordinate is irrelevant, so we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/9/4e9f98fc1f8b9fa7a14068ea8de7479dd6a4e617.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E(y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> be the expected value of the number of jumps it will take him to reach the river from a given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-coordinate. Observe that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/a/68a7cd558ff4195c20e6462d1909470e26a35854.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E(24)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/9/4b9ff253dde871e82bb01432210d99e3e96a597e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[E(y)=1+\\frac{E(y+1)+E(y-1)+2E(y)}{4}\\]\" width=\"326\" height=\"39\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/a/28a60ba0c70283bd1dc8acbfd632e0f9a4d77de6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\le y\\le 23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" />. Also note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/2/90208a0cc480ccd3e2e17b0dce90ef754a76b050.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E(0)=1+\\frac{2E(0)+E(1)}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"202\" height=\"38\" />. This gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/1/96114c440addd1d2604e9f91914bebed3343d9aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E(0)=E(1)+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"130\" height=\"18\" />. Plugging this into the equation for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/6/346120bd39724616834486ae4d902a8e0aa7d01e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> gives that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/7/ca7d9dba0e1f44b02201911f9128a809412cd9a8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[E(1)=1+\\frac{E(2)+3E(1)+3}{4},\\]\" width=\"238\" height=\"39\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/5/c850ef6f7f337eb277ca12dd52758e7d7232ad50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E(1)=E(2)+7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"131\" height=\"18\" />. Iteratively plugging this in gives that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/6/806e40a03ef8291747a2dc0c090f2404d7adf87f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E(n)=E(n+1)+4n+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"207\" height=\"18\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/b/9bb9bbaa47d001f5dbd937b7d71429dcaeaf275b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E(23)=E(24)+95$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"157\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/2/91274e82affd2bf5a0f9f352cb494e7f26003b81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E(22)=E(23)+91=E(24)+186$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"278\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/b/36b49758a29e04d287564c2615bd1803c441e182.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E(21)=E(22)+87=E(24)+273=\\boxed{273}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"342\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Cancellation.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Cancellation)\">Solution 2 (Cancellation)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Cancellation)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As in Solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/9/4e9f98fc1f8b9fa7a14068ea8de7479dd6a4e617.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E(y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> be the expected value of jumps it takes Freddy to reach the river from the specific <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> coordinate. We can set up a system of equations. The equation for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/f/61f29a97115cb7a44341dc2b5e19cba4e53ff55c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E(0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/9/bf97e380c0c5c5b5357266c3ad4bb347147e24ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E(0)=\\frac{2}{3}(E(0)+1)+\\frac{1}{3}(E(1)+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"278\" height=\"38\" />, which, rearranging, gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/7/bf76af951b7a2d1c949ac787c637408706a542d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E(0)=E(1)+3.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"138\" height=\"20\" /> The equation for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/e/92e6ad43219e04601b59b88bf2d9a914a92ec5ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E(23)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"49\" height=\"20\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/7/687c58b260ba1cfbb1c78ce7271e7ae40169990c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E(23)=\\frac{1}{2}(E(23)+1)+\\frac{1}{4}(E(22)+1)+\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"341\" height=\"38\" /> (since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/a/68a7cd558ff4195c20e6462d1909470e26a35854.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E(24)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" />), and rearranging gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/4/0d42b3ee44c3f3052f8d7dcb5b3eff9c9320ae9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2E(23)=E(22)+4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"160\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nFor any other <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/7/ce70473d9e9b1e278c8370578a20eac42e37e254.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;y&lt;23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"17\" />, we can get the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/6/d8648ab2350e7e3f85f38404f90123fd53862cd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E(y)=\\frac{1}{2}(E(y)+1)+\\frac{1}{4}(E(y-1)+1)+\\frac{1}{4}(E(y+1)+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"461\" height=\"38\" />, which can be rearranged to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/8/2d877c6b13431abc269e88c1d1b2d148c871cdd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2E(y)=E(y-1)+E(y+1)+4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"266\" height=\"20\" />. Thus, we can get the following system of equations:\n\\begin{align*}\n2E(23)&amp;=E(22)+4\\\\\n2E(22)&amp;=E(21)+E(23)+4\\\\\n2E(21)&amp;=E(20)+E(22)+4\\\\\n.\\\\\n.\\\\\n.\\\\\n2E(2)&amp;=E(1)+E(3)+4\\\\\n2E(1)&amp;=E(0)+E(2)+4\\\\\nE(0)&amp;=E(1)+3.\n\\end{align*}\n</p><p>Adding all the equations and cancelling results in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/a/ffabd744d3542c95d62f98d4d24847a4cafc0958.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E(23)=3+4(23)=95$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"188\" height=\"20\" />. From the first equation, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/a/e7aa829b1af962f1c945d964669c79e16dd316ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E(22)=2\\cdot 95-4=186$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"196\" height=\"20\" />, and from the second equation, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/7/ad79998851399f30a201ad5b01ceb431f6e5820e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E(21)=2\\cdot 186-95-4=\\boxed{273}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"262\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~The_Other_Guy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/T5F4e8NxfG0\">https://youtu.be/T5F4e8NxfG0</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For those who want more explanation, here is a video explaining the solution: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jQCGkOGMlFQ\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jQCGkOGMlFQ</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I\" title=\"2016 AIME I\">2016 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2016 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2016\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018001000\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.044 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.064 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 277/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1790/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 112/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7030/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.268      1 -total\n 60.09%    8.573      1 Template:AIME_box\n 37.85%    5.401      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:14843:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018001000 and revision id 284338. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}